      "autoClaim:1": 0,
      "desc:8": "Time to cut the cord. An Antenna T1 Head tops a guyed mast of 6 to 32 Steel Frame Boxes, a dipole under the head and three guys down to LV Machine Casing anchors; its Energy Hatch goes in the equipment shelter in front. It uses 32 EU/t.%n%nIt reaches about 64 blocks on open ground. Height helps; hills and roofs cost you signal. Antennas find each other on their own, but radio links carry little. Wire it to a pylon, a terminal or an Exchange within 16 blocks, with cable in your hotbar, and it carries all 4 of its calls over the wire.%n%nMore in the guide: [guide page=becom:antennas.md]Antennas[/guide].",
